From: Captain-Tripps
Subject: [PATCH] sycl verify: batch_poll: test the copy stream's empty() result, not its error code

Verifier::batch_poll checks whether the copy stream still has work before it
reports a batched window as done:

    const dpct::err0 qc = DPCT_CHECK_ERROR(copy_->ext_oneapi_empty());
    if (qc == 1) return 0;

DPCT_CHECK_ERROR returns 0 unless the call throws, so qc is always 0 and the
check never fires. When the compute queue has drained but copy_ still has
work, the poll returns "done" and the caller goes on to ep_check /
sample_rows / reading b_out_. The sibling check on the compute queue a few
lines up was already written as `empty() ? 0 : 1`; this one was missed.

Measured (Windows, 2x Arc Pro B70, Qwen3.8-Flash-Next IQ3_S, served, A/B/A/B,
9 requests per round): speeds equal (19.7k prompt 2,410 tok/s both, decode
97.6-156.9 both) and draft-accepted counts identical on every request. No
failure was seen without the fix, probably because copy_ normally finishes
first. A correctness cleanup, not a speed change.

---
diff --git a/sycl/src/core/verify.cpp b/sycl/src/core/verify.cpp
index 8cac6af..a684704 100644
--- a/sycl/src/core/verify.cpp
+++ b/sycl/src/core/verify.cpp
@@ -4094,8 +4094,7 @@ int Verifier::batch_poll(PoolMultiFn pool, void *user, std::string &err) try {
       b_running_ = false;
       return -1;
     }
-    const dpct::err0 qc = DPCT_CHECK_ERROR(
-        ((copy_)->ext_oneapi_empty())); // no host function of this window may
+    const dpct::err0 qc = (copy_)->ext_oneapi_empty() ? 0 : 1; // no host function of this window may
                                         // raise flag B in the next
     /*
     DPCT1001: The statement could not be removed.
